# Per-machine state an assistant CLI keeps for this project. The one that was tracked
# here was a symlink into a home directory, so it reached the server as a dangling link
# and then the image. The `*ignore` files and the `*.md` instructions beside them are
# real project configuration and stay versioned; this is not.
.antigravitycli/

# Copies the download targets leave behind before overwriting, named with `BACKUP_SUFFIX`
# in the Makefile. `download-media` alone drops 45 MB in the working tree, which is exactly
# the kind of thing `git add -A` sweeps in.
*.backup.*
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Project specific
# External channel-link data sources (see AGENTS.md): never commit them
screenshot*.png
*.m3u
# Input for addlinksource: external data, never part of the repository.
newera.txt
elcano.txt
soccertime_data_cache.sqlite
# Anchored, because a `.gitignore` pattern with no slash is matched against every path
# segment at every depth: bare `media` and `db` were written for these two directories at
# the root and also hid any directory of those names anywhere else in the tree. Nothing in
# the Python project is called either, which is why it never showed.
/media/
/db/
/static/
.env.production.local
.docker/traefik/certs/mojon.local.key
.docker/traefik/certs/mojon.local.crt

# The Android project under `android/`. Gradle writes its caches and its output inside the
# tree it builds, and one debug APK is larger than everything else here put together.
# `build/` above is deliberately left unanchored: that is what covers every module's output.
android/.gradle/
android/.kotlin/
android/.cxx/
android/captures/
android/local.properties
android/**/build/
*.apk
*.aab
# Signing material. The release keystore never enters the repository — CI holds it as a
# base64 secret, and AGENTS.md says how it is made.
*.jks
*.keystore

# Claude Code per-machine state. Project-wide configuration belongs in
# .claude/settings.json, which stays tracked so it can be shared.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/.cc-writes/
backups/
